----OCI Architecture----
REGION --> AD --> FD

Choosing a region: 
 1. Location
 2. Data residency & compliance
 3. Service Availability 

Availability Domain: Isolated from each other, fault toleance, unlikily to fail simultaniuosly. 
 - Each availability Domain has three FD
 - Logical data center within an AD

FD: A fault domain is a subdivision of an AD. Each availability domain contains three fault domains. Fault domains let you distribute your instances so that they are not on the same physical hardware within a single availability domain. A fault domain cannot be associated with multiple availability domains.


-----Identity and Access Management-----
Authentication: who is going to login (users)
Authorization: Permissions

Identity Domain:
 - users, groups, --> policies --> compartment --> resources.

Compartments:
 - Logical containers 
 - All compartments are global. 
 - Six level of nesting. 
 - we can set quotas & budgets. 
Ex: Compartment A [VM's, Virtual cloud Network, Load Balancer]

Principals: IAM entities that are allows to interact with OCI resources. 
 1. IAM Users
 2. Resource principals
 3. Group
